# The build context is this directory (Dockerfile.trading's header says why),
# so this file is the trading image's own - the repository root's
# ../../.dockerignore never applies to it.
#
# Everything here is either regenerated inside the image or has no business in
# one. .venv is the expensive entry: it holds the linters and pyright's
# bundled Node, a few hundred megabytes uploaded to the daemon for an image
# that builds its own environment from uv.lock anyway.
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache

# Written into the image by the build itself, from the AERIE_REVISION build
# arg. A copy from a developer's machine would be a stale stamp that looks
# exactly like a real one - which is the failure aerie_trading/revision.py
# exists to make impossible.
aerie_trading/build.json

# The tests never run in the image - that is the CI lane's job - and nothing in
# it imports them. README.md is deliberately *not* excluded: pyproject.toml
# names it as the distribution's readme, so hatchling refuses to build the
# project without it.
tests
